id: jf-axko
title: Add version-aware Jellyfin API compatibility manifests
description: "Add a read-only agent-first compatibility surface that compares the configured live OpenAPI contract with trusted official stable or explicitly opted-in preview schemas, classifies operation and component-schema drift, emits schema-validated structured formats, and supports CI breaking-change gates without exposing private server data."
type: Plan
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[7]: agents,api,compatibility,openapi,read-only,release,schema
created_at: "2026-07-25T00:14:27.009Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T01:13:22.169Z"
assignee: codex-jellyfin-compat
author: codex-jellyfin-compat
estimated_minutes: 600
acceptance_criteria: Default comparison uses the configured live document and its exact official stable version without forwarding credentials; Explicit version comparison supports Jellyfin 12 prerelease only with an opt-in flag and validates official source identity; Operation additions removals identifier changes parameter requiredness body and response drift plus component schema drift are deterministically classified; TOON JSON YAML Markdown table and raw formats are schema-valid and documented with detailed nested help; A fail-on-breaking CI mode returns nonzero only after emitting a complete machine-readable report; Unit integration installed-package and private compiled live read-only acceptance pass with no secrets or live mutations
goal: jf-mqpo
value: Let agents and maintainers reason about upgrades and server-specific API drift before invoking operations.
impact: Prevents silent API incompatibility across Jellyfin stable upgrades previews and plugin-extended local servers.
outcome: A deterministic privacy-safe compatibility manifest and CI gate for current and future Jellyfin API contracts.
why_now: The exact-operation fallback provides reach but agents still lack evidence about version drift and breaking contract changes; Jellyfin 12 RC3 makes this gap immediate.
parent: jf-gn5j
reviewer: github-review-bots
risk: high
confidence: high
sprint: jellyfin-10.11.11-to-12
release: next-manual-release
