comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T00:14:27.009Z",codex-jellyfin-compat,Search across all 41 PM items found the related exact-operation and fallback lineage but no version-aware compatibility manifest item. This plan is the sole active in-progress item; the broader coverage and static-quality features remain open and unclaimed.
  "2026-07-25T00:36:29.159Z",codex-jellyfin-compat,The first full release run passed 939 Bun tests but correctly failed on a Vitest unhandled EADDRINUSE after all 930 assertions. Root cause was random fixed-port selection in the Node Bun.serve compatibility adapter; parallel workers could choose the same port. Replaced it with deterministic per-process allocation and restarted the entire release gate.
  "2026-07-25T00:39:20.737Z",codex-jellyfin-compat,"The second complete release run confirmed the port-collision fix, then failed because one new test serialized four CLI subprocess format checks and exceeded Vitest's 5-second default under full-suite load. Parallelized the independent checks and assigned a bounded 15-second test timeout; three consecutive focused portable runs passed. Restarting the entire release gate again."
  "2026-07-25T00:42:10.875Z",codex-jellyfin-compat,"Full release validator passed after deterministic test-server port isolation and bounded parallel formatter checks: 939 Bun tests passed (180 read-only live tests intentionally skipped in offline validator), 930 Vitest tests passed, 9 release tests passed, build/package-installed npm exec/Bun smoke/file-length/secret scans/changelog check all passed. Separate four-metric coverage remains an honest repository baseline of 39.44% statements, 39.52% branches, 50.77% functions, and 39.05% lines; canonical coverage work remains jf-mkzh. Strict zero-duplication gate also remains open at 8.62% lines / 8.49% tokens (219 clones); canonical deduplication work remains jf-lpki. This plan does not weaken, exclude, or misreport either gate."
  "2026-07-25T00:52:09.376Z",codex-jellyfin-compat,PM-linked acceptance added realistic full-suite load and exposed the first compatibility test still using Vitest's 5-second default while running three actual CLI subprocesses. The same PM run proved focused 34/34 and compiled private live read-only 180/180. Set the behavior-focused test's explicit bound to 15 seconds without changing assertions or production behavior; three consecutive portable focused runs now pass. Re-running all linked PM tests for a clean tracker-native record.
  "2026-07-25T01:00:00.578Z",codex-jellyfin-compat,"The second PM-linked run correctly categorized a different existing schema-suite failure as an infrastructure collision. Root cause: PID-derived fixed-port ranges were not globally collision-free. The portable Bun.serve adapter now asks the OS for a real ephemeral port and reads the immediately bound wildcard TCP address before returning; this preserves the synchronous Bun.serve test contract and removes guessed ports. Three consecutive complete portable runs pass 930/930. Re-running tracker-native acceptance."
  "2026-07-25T01:05:57.561Z",codex-jellyfin-compat,"Third tracker-native run passed all 930 portable assertions, build, packaging, security, and smoke stages, then hit the already-reported pm-cli tracker-sandbox changelog identity defect unbraind/pm-cli#682; the same changelog check passes directly with exact 37-item parity. Its subsequent focused run exposed one remaining default 5-second bound under tracker load, so every compatibility test that spawns the actual CLI now has the same explicit 15-second upper bound. Live compiled acceptance again passed 180/180. No duplicate pm-cli issue created because #682 is canonical."
  "2026-07-25T01:13:22.169Z",codex-jellyfin-compat,"Final semantic review expanded drift detection to inline request content and response schemas plus non-breaking requiredness relaxations, and moved the fully constrained compatibility output contract into a dedicated under-300-LOC schema module. Focused Bun/Vitest pass 9/9, full release passes 940 Bun + 931 Vitest + 9 release tests, and the rebuilt actual CLI re-passed the live exact-stable compatibility acceptance under read-only mode."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T00:14:27.009Z",codex-jellyfin-compat,"Privacy boundary: credentials, local URLs, raw live schemas, entity data, and cache paths remain only under owner-only ~/.jellyfin-cli. PM, git, PR, and docs may contain official versions, contract categories, and aggregate counts only."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T00:14:27.009Z",codex-jellyfin-compat,Official Jellyfin 12.0 RC3 is intentionally stored in the stable OpenAPI artifact directory but reports info.version 12.0.0; source artifact identity and document API version must therefore be represented separately.
