plan_mode: executing
plan_scope: "Official/live OpenAPI acquisition, normalized compatibility manifests, breaking-risk classification, command help and schemas, documentation, tests, private live stable/preview acceptance, and production PR closeout."
plan_harness: codex
plan_resume_context: "Stable Jellyfin is 10.11.11 and the local owner-only server matches it; 12.0 RC3 is prerelease. Exact operation execution shipped in jf-0ea5. Add a non-duplicative schema compatibility command with stable defaults, explicit prerelease opt-in, no auth forwarding to official origins, and honest breaking-risk classification."
plan_decisions[1]{ts,author,decision,rationale,evidence}:
  "2026-07-25T00:30:06.312Z",codex-jellyfin-compat,Use official current-version baseline by default and require --baseline live for plugin drift.,This prevents installed plugin endpoints from being mislabeled as core removals in a Jellyfin upgrade report while retaining a deliberate server-extension audit.,Sanitized live-to-official 10.11.11 comparison reported 41 operation and 21 schema removals that disappear from the core 10.11.11-to-12.0 RC3 baseline.
plan_discoveries[1]{ts,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T00:30:04.571Z",codex-jellyfin-compat,The live 10.11.11 schema includes 41 operations and 21 component schemas beyond the official core artifact because installed plugins extend the contract. Upgrade analysis must default to official-to-official comparison while live drift remains an explicit mode.
